Ubuntu packaging of the original upstream release
=================================================

This branch starts directly at upstream Ares v148, commit
0aafd85789215e84e1e43415c07d4c88461b7899. Upstream commits retain their
original identities. Debian/Salsa supplies packaging knowledge and derived
files, not Git ancestry. The initial import was taken from Salsa master at
15e2123befb01e87c85e1e42722d7f477b456e62; its complete changelog is preserved.

The upstream source is intact: no +dfsg repack, Files-Excluded, source patches,
or unvendoring. libchdr and its LZMA, miniz and zstd dependencies are built from
thirdparty/. debian/source/format is 3.0 (quilt), with no patch series.
License notices and the unresolved provenance of embedded firmware are recorded
in debian/copyright; firmware permissions need separate verification before
redistribution.

This Ubuntu 24.04 Noble package is a v148 baseline for investigating a later
upstream performance regression. Emulation features are unchanged. Actual
Mega Drive performance must be checked by the user on their target machine.

Build variants
==============

All builds use ARES_BUILD_LOCAL=OFF to avoid -march=native, and
ARES_SKIP_DEPS=ON to prevent fetching upstream prebuilt dependencies.
ARES_ENABLE_MINIMUM_CPU=OFF lets packaging control instruction-set baselines.
Normal builds use upstream RelWithDebInfo; DEB_BUILD_OPTIONS=noopt selects Debug.
Hardening and QA flags are supplied by dpkg-buildflags.

amd64: build ares-no-simd with -march=x86-64 and ares-simd with -march=x86-64-v2.
Both live in /usr/libexec/ares/. /usr/bin/ares queries
/lib64/ld-linux-x86-64.so.2 --help under LC_ALL=C and uses exec to launch the
appropriate binary, forwarding every argument unchanged.

arm64: NEON is guaranteed by the architecture baseline, so only ares-simd is
built. /usr/bin/ares is a symlink to it.

Other architectures supported by upstream: build only ares-no-simd, with
/usr/bin/ares as a symlink. Nintendo 64 is included only on amd64/arm64.
Mega Drive requires compiler support for __int128. Foreign architectures have
not been validated by the initial native amd64 build.

Each variant is installed into its own temporary staging root. Keep the binary
from each, but install /usr/share only once: from SIMD on amd64/arm64, otherwise
from no-SIMD. Remove both remaining variant roots before dh_install. The
sourcery resource compiler is a build tool and is excluded from the package.

Build dependencies
==================

CMake >= 3.28 is required by upstream. Use GTK3, OpenGL/X11 and the ALSA,
PulseAudio, OpenAL, libao, SDL3 and udev backends. Noble needs an available SDL3
backport. libchdr-dev, GtkSourceView and Xv are not build dependencies.
The optional librashader runtime is not required; upstream's bundled header
loader supports environments without it.

Use the user's deb-packages/deb_builder.yml for local Noble validation with
upload_to_ppa=false, sign_source_package=false and run_sbuild_verification=true.
The orig tarball must be generated from v148 with no exclusions. The builder
may stage packaging separately but must not change this upstream source.
